    "lawCode": "Amd §§3216, 3221 & 4303, Ins L",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S3654A\n\nSPONSOR: BAILEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the insurance law, in relation to requiring health\ninsurers to provide coverage for speech therapy for stuttering\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to grant insurance coverage for those\nsuffering from stuttering.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill amends the insurance law to require insurers to provide cover-\nage for costs related to stuttering, including speech therapy.  Such\ntreatment must be recommended by a licensed health care provider. The\nact would apply to policies and contracts that are issued on or after\nthe effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMillions of Americans suffer from stuttering. Stuttering can occur in\nchildhood or can result from an underlying adverse medical condition or\noccurrence, such as a stroke or a brain injury. Stuttering can also\ndevelop due to the genetic predisposition of the person, their neurophy-\nsiology, and even family dynamics. Unfortunately, not all insurers\nprovide coverage for this condition. This bill, which is patterned after\nsimilar legislation in other states, will ensure that stuttering is\ncovered throughout our state.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATION FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nOne hundred twenty days after becoming a law, with provisions.\n",
